      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2019-june/q1",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)=z^4+az^3+bz^2+cz+d\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> are real constants.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1+2\\mathrm i\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3-\\mathrm i\"></span> are two roots of the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)=0\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show all the roots of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)=0\"></span> on a single Argand diagram, <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
