      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2019-june/q3",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:110mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-01-2019-june/q03-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1: rectangle ABCD with AB = 1.2 m; inside it a closed peanut-shaped curve touching all four sides, the region between the curve and the rectangle shaded; marked Diagram not to scale.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows the design for a table top in the shape of a rectangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCD\"></span>. The length of the table, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span>, is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.2\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>. The area inside the closed curve is made of glass and the surrounding area, shown shaded in Figure 1, is made of wood.</p><p>The perimeter of the glass is modelled by the curve with polar equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=0.4+a\\cos 2\\theta\\qquad 0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=0.2\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Hence, given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AD=60\\,\\mathrm{cm}\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>find the area of the wooden part of the table top, giving your answer in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm m^2\"></span> to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(8)</span></li></ol>",
