      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2019-june/q4",
      "question": "<p>Prove that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\in\\mathbb Z\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\geqslant 0\"></span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=0}^{n}\\frac{1}{(r+1)(r+2)(r+3)}=\\frac{(n+a)(n+b)}{c(n+2)(n+3)}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are integers to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
