      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2019-june/q7",
      "question": "<p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{-1}=\\frac{z-4}{3}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\mathbf i+3\\mathbf k+t(\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j+2\\mathbf k)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is a scalar parameter.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> lie in the same plane. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Write down a vector equation for the plane containing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>Find, to the nearest degree, the acute angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
